id:                     E1617
trigger_tool: conan|runtime|consumer-test
phase: installed-package-validation
error_signature: consumer enters main and version check passes, then crashes at constructor requiring a global event loop
severity:               2
category:               conan, runtime, dependency-initialization
match_keywords: default event loop, dependency context, constructor segfault, aml_get_default, consumer test, upstream example
title: Initialize required dependency context before constructing an installed library object
root_cause: A consumer can link and load a packaged library correctly while omitting a dependency's process-local default context. When the public constructor immediately dereferences that context, the test crashes even though packaging and dynamic loading have succeeded.
affected_scope: Event-driven C libraries whose constructors use a global or thread-local default scheduler, event loop, allocator, or context supplied by a separately packaged dependency.
verification_cmd: Compare the library constructor with upstream examples, initialize and register the required default context in the consumer, run the installed-package test, then unregister and release the context after object destruction.
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: dependency-context-first-consumer
rec_description: Bind the context dependency explicitly in test_package, create and set its default before constructing the tested object, then destroy the object before clearing and releasing the context. Keep this test separate from the upstream test count.
rec_command: Inspect constructor and official example call order; run a fresh target Conan create with the corrected consumer and verify upstream and consumer totals independently.
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: consumer-fixture-and-dependency-graph
forbid_1_pattern: constructor crash.*packaging failure
forbid_1_reason: A successful main entry and library version read prove loading already succeeded; a crash at the context dereference is a consumer setup error.
forbid_1_consequence: Re-signing or relinking the package repeatedly does not initialize the missing runtime context.
principles:               
